WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.993
Will two substances react? Table 4 answers it with one rule.

00:00:05.593 --> 00:00:19.165
A reaction happens when the oxidising agent is lower in the table than the reducing agent. The electrons run downhill: from a stronger reducing agent, high on the right, to a stronger oxidising agent, low on the left.

00:00:21.665 --> 00:00:24.485
A piece of zinc is placed in copper sulfate solution.

00:00:25.085 --> 00:00:38.055
The oxidising agent is the copper two plus ion, at plus zero comma three four volts. Compare it with the oxidising agent in zinc's own row, the zinc two plus ion, at minus zero comma seven six volts.

00:00:38.655 --> 00:00:49.570
Copper two plus is lower in the table, so it is the stronger oxidising agent. It oxidises the zinc. A reddish-brown layer of copper forms, and the blue colour fades.

00:00:52.070 --> 00:01:00.554
Now a silver wire is placed in iron two sulfate solution. Will it react? Decide, and say why in one sentence.

00:01:06.154 --> 00:01:19.746
No reaction. Iron two plus, at minus zero comma four four volts, is a weaker oxidising agent than silver plus, at plus zero comma eight zero volts. So iron two plus cannot oxidise silver.

00:01:22.246 --> 00:01:31.070
The memos want a sentence with named species and the words stronger or weaker. X is a stronger oxidising agent than Y, so X oxidises Z.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:39.067
Compare like with like: two oxidising agents, or two reducing agents. And use the agents the question names.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:50.711
Saying that silver is less reactive names no agent and gives no strength. When a question says, use the relative strengths, that answer earns nothing.

00:01:53.211 --> 00:02:09.428
Remember that every solution contains water. An iron nail in copper sulfate reduces the copper ions, not the water. The water row, at minus zero comma eight three volts, is above the iron row, so water is too weak an oxidising agent to react with iron.

00:02:11.928 --> 00:02:20.474
Open the test-tube lab in Predict mode. For each tube, decide yes or no, write your sentence, and only then watch what happens.
